        "marks": 1
       },
       {
        "id": "p4",
        "description": "A1 simplifies to the given result.",
        "marks": 1
       }
      ]
     },
     "modelAnswer": "$$\nS_n = \\frac{1}{2}\\sum_{r=1}^{n}\\left[\\frac{1}{r(r + 1)} - \\frac{1}{(r + 1)(r + 2)}\\right]\n$$\n\n$$\n= \\frac{1}{2}\\left[\\left(\\frac{1}{1 \\cdot 2} - \\frac{1}{2 \\cdot 3}\\right) + \\left(\\frac{1}{2 \\cdot 3} - \\frac{1}{3 \\cdot 4}\\right) + \\cdots + \\left(\\frac{1}{n(n + 1)} - \\frac{1}{(n + 1)(n + 2)}\\right)\\right]\n$$\n\n$$\n= \\frac{1}{2}\\left[\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{(n + 1)(n + 2)}\\right] = \\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{1}{2(n + 1)(n + 2)}\n$$"
